{%- comment -%}
  Where a "shortcut" (a quick filter chip, a "See beds like this" link)
  should take the shopper, worked out from the store's real filters.

  1. When Search & Discovery offers the matching filter on this list
     (results.filters), the link applies it in place: the filter value's own
     url_to_add, which keeps every filter and the sort already chosen. When
     that value is already applied, the link removes it instead.
  2. Otherwise, the fallback collection, if it has products, is not the
     page you are on, and shares at least one bed with it.
  3. Otherwise nothing: the caller hides the shortcut, so it never leads to
     an empty page or to the page you are already on.

  So the metafield filters start working on their own once the owner adds
  them in Search & Discovery; until then the shortcuts go to collections.

  Parameters
    results     collection (or search) whose filters to use (required)
    key         which filter (see below), or 'none' for collection only
    price       for key 'price_under': the price ceiling in whole pounds
    fallback    a collection object to use when the filter is not there

  Keys
    low_entry · has_liner · non_slip           boolean product metafields (custom.*)
    memory_foam · egg_crate                    custom.core_type value
    curls_up · head_on_edge · stretches_out    custom.sleep_style value
    weight_25_40 · weight_40                   variant custom.suits_weight value
    price_under                                Shopify's price filter (filter.v.price.lte)

  Output: "mode|url" with mode add (applies a filter here), remove (the
  filter is on; the link takes it off) or collection (goes elsewhere).
  Nothing when there is nowhere useful to go. Capture and split on '|':
    {%- capture hit -%}{%- render 'col-filter-link', results: collection, key: 'low_entry', fallback: c -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cf_param = ''
  assign cf_value = ''
  assign cf_bool = false
  case key
    when 'low_entry', 'has_liner', 'non_slip'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.' | append: key
      assign cf_bool = true
    when 'memory_foam'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.core_type'
      assign cf_value = 'Memory foam'
    when 'egg_crate'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.core_type'
      assign cf_value = 'Egg-crate foam'
    when 'curls_up'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.sleep_style'
      assign cf_value = 'Curls up'
    when 'head_on_edge'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.sleep_style'
      assign cf_value = 'Head on the edge'
    when 'stretches_out'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.p.m.custom.sleep_style'
      assign cf_value = 'Stretches out'
    when 'weight_25_40'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.v.m.custom.suits_weight'
      assign cf_value = '25–40kg'
    when 'weight_40'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.v.m.custom.suits_weight'
      assign cf_value = '40kg+'
    when 'price_under'
      assign cf_param = 'filter.v.price'
  endcase

  assign cf_out = ''
  if cf_param != '' and results.filters.size > 0
    for cf_filter in results.filters
      if cf_param == 'filter.v.price'
        if cf_filter.type == 'price_range'
          assign cf_max = price | default: 0 | plus: 0
          if cf_max > 0
            assign cf_cents = cf_max | times: 100
            assign cf_on = false
            if cf_filter.max_value.value == cf_cents and cf_filter.min_value.value == nil
              assign cf_on = true
            endif
            if cf_on
              assign cf_out = 'remove|' | append: cf_filter.url_to_remove
            else
              assign cf_base = cf_filter.url_to_remove | default: results.url
              if cf_base contains '?'
                assign cf_join = '&'
              else
                assign cf_join = '?'
              endif
              assign cf_out = 'add|' | append: cf_base | append: cf_join | append: 'filter.v.price.lte=' | append: cf_max
            endif
          endif
          break
        endif
      elsif cf_filter.param_name == cf_param
        for cf_v in cf_filter.values
          assign cf_hit = false
          if cf_bool
            if cf_v.value == '1' or cf_v.value == 'true'
              assign cf_hit = true
            endif
          elsif cf_v.value == cf_value
            assign cf_hit = true
          endif
          if cf_hit
            if cf_v.active
              assign cf_out = 'remove|' | append: cf_v.url_to_remove
            elsif cf_v.count > 0
              assign cf_out = 'add|' | append: cf_v.url_to_add
            endif
            break
          endif
        endfor
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    The fallback collection must share a bed with the page on screen, so a
    kennels page never offers "Memory foam" beds elsewhere.
  endcomment
  if cf_out == '' and fallback != blank
    if fallback.all_products_count > 0 and fallback.handle != collection.handle
      assign cf_overlap = true
      if collection.handle != blank and collection.handle != 'all'
        assign cf_overlap = false
        for cf_p in fallback.products limit: 50
          for cf_c in cf_p.collections
            if cf_c.handle == collection.handle
              assign cf_overlap = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
          if cf_overlap
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endif
      if cf_overlap
        assign cf_out = 'collection|' | append: fallback.url
      endif
    endif
  endif

  echo cf_out
-%}
